%S A102628 1,1,2,2,6,2,14,10,19,13,55,22,100,51,79,113,296,130,489,219,407,441,
%T A102628 1254,544,1552,1111,2006,1400,4564,1527,6841,4163,5842,5845,9634,6037,
%U A102628 21636,12499,18522,15487,44582,14140,63260,30749,46977,51488,124753
%N A102628 Number of partitions of n in which the number of parts is relatively prime to n.
%C A102628 By conjugation, a(n) is also the number of partitions of n whose largest part is coprime to n. For prime p, a(p) = A000041(p) - 1, since the only partition of p into p parts is 1 + 1 + ... + 1. - _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 12 2026
%H A102628 Pierre Colmant, <a href="/A102628/b102628.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%F A102628 a(n) = Sum_{k=1..n, gcd(k,n)=1} A008284(n,k). - _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 12 2026
%e A102628 a(4) = 2: the partitions of 4 into a number of parts coprime to 4 are 4 (1 part) and 2+1+1 (3 parts). - _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 12 2026
%o A102628 (Python)
%o A102628 from math import gcd
%o A102628 from sympy.utilities.iterables import partitions
%o A102628 def A102628(n): return sum(1 for p in partitions(n) if gcd(sum(p.values()), n) == 1)
%o A102628 # _Pierre Colmant_, Nov 12 2026
%Y A102628 Cf. A000041, A008284.
%K A102628 easy,nonn,changed
